  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on interviews with industry stakeholders rather than direct engagement with homeowners themselves.",
      "what": "This study identifies barriers to residential energy retrofits and strategies for homeowner engagement by conducting semi-structured interviews with 40 retrofit industry stakeholders. The findings outline a shift from investment-focused to consumption-focused marketing, a transition from property-centred to homeowner-centred delivery models, and the implementation of socially contextualised neighbourhood-scale approaches.",
      "why": "It reframes retrofit delivery from a top-down, technical-rational model to one aligned with homeowner behaviour and local social contexts, offering empirical strategies to overcome the stagnation of residential decarbonisation programs."
    }
